Output: Kinetic Energy = 225.0
(0.5 * 4.5 * 10 * 10 = 225.0. Writing 1/2 * m * v * v would give 0.0, because 1/2 is integer division = 0.)

class Kinetic
{
    public static void main(String args[])
    {
        double m = 4.5;            // mass in kg
        double v = 10.0;           // velocity in m/s
        double ke = 0.5 * m * v * v;   // K.E. = 1/2 m v^2
        System.out.println("Kinetic Energy = " + ke);
    }
}

/* Variable description
   m  : double : mass of the body (kg)
   v  : double : velocity of the body (m/s)
   ke : double : computed kinetic energy */

